{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.exp_pow_even_not_isZeta4Faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.exp_pow_even_not_isZeta4Faithful","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L141-L153","doc":"**The concrete refutation.** No **even** power (`m > 0`) of the ζ₄-faithful\ncarrier `exp` is itself ζ₄-faithful: if it were, `pow_even_isZeta4Faithful_eq_zero`\nat `z = 0` would give `(exp 0)ᵐ = 1ᵐ = 1 = 0`, false. This is the Arm-2 pincer\napplied to a genuine faithful carrier — the even-degree pure-power monomial\nf-maps are excluded on the faithful arm (bean `5nx8` `IsZeta4Faithful`), no\nanchor sweep, no c_k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.pow_even_isZeta4Faithful_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.pow_even_isZeta4Faithful_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L127-L139","doc":"**Even monomial powers of a ζ₄-faithful carrier vanish (over ℂ).** If `A` is\na `zeta4Rot`-eigenfunction with eigenvalue `i` and the even power `Aᵐ` is\n`IsZeta4Faithful`, then `(A z)ᵐ = 0` for every `z`. (`4 ≠ 0` in ℂ upgrades the\ngeneric `4·Aᵐ = 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.exp_isEigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.exp_isEigen","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L123-L125","doc":"`Complex.exp` is a `zeta4Rot`-eigenfunction with eigenvalue `i` (repackaging\n`exp_zeta4_eigen`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.pow_even_faithful_four_mul_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.pow_even_faithful_four_mul_zero","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**Pincer Arm-2 core.** For a `ζ₄` eigenfunction (`ζ² = −1`) and an **even**\npower `m`, ζ₄-faithfulness of the monomial power `Aᵐ` (both non-faithful orbit\nsums vanish) forces `4·Aᵐ ≡ 0`. Because `m` is even, `μ = ζᵐ` has `μ² = ζ²ᵐ =\n(ζ²)ᵐ = (−1)ᵐ = 1`, so the isotype collapse fires. Generic `[CommRing R]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.four_mul_eq_zero_of_eigen_sq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.four_mul_eq_zero_of_eigen_sq_one","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L79-L96","doc":"**Isotype collapse.** Let `g` be a `rot`-eigenfunction with eigenvalue `μ`,\n`μ² = 1`. If both non-faithful ℤ₄ orbit sums vanish — the trivial isotype\n`g z + g(rot z) + g(rot² z) + g(rot³ z)` and the sign isotype\n`g z − g(rot z) + g(rot² z) − g(rot³ z)` — then `4·g z = 0`. (With `μ² = 1` the\ntwo sums are `2(1+μ)·g z` and `2(1−μ)·g z`; their sum is `4·g z`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.eigen_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.eigen_pow","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L70-L77","doc":"**Eigenvalue of a monomial power.** If `A` is a `rot`-eigenfunction with\neigenvalue `ζ`, then the pointwise power `Aᵐ` is a `rot`-eigenfunction with\neigenvalue `ζᵐ`: `Aᵐ(rot z) = (ζ·A z)ᵐ = ζᵐ·Aᵐ z`. Pure algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.IsEigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.IsEigen","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QbetaFmapPowerClassPrune.lean#L64-L68","doc":"A function `A : X → R` is an **eigenfunction** of a self-map `rot : X → X`\nwith eigenvalue `ζ` iff `A (rot z) = ζ · A z` for all `z`. This abstracts the\n`ζ₄ = i` rotation `z ↦ z + iπ/2` of the fibre argument (whose `exp`-eigenfunction\nis `exp_zeta4_eigen` in `ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}